% Copyright (C) 2026 Chris Arena and Claude Opus 5, 2026-10-16.
% GPL-2.0-only, the same terms as the tree this exercises;
% see COPYING at the top of it.  Not part of LADR-2009-11A.
%------------------------------------------------------------------------------
% M7 -- a heap buffer overflow on every production-mode run.
%
% This file is LADR (prover9) input, not TPTP, because the defect is in the
% prover rather than the translator.  It is six lines long and it overflows
% the heap on the 2009 code.
%
% THE DEFECT
%   ladr/dollar.c sized an array from the symbol count and then filled it
%   using calls that ADD to that count:
%
%       Symbols_size = greatest_symnum() + 1;          /* a snapshot */
%       Op_codes = calloc(Symbols_size, sizeof(int));
%       Op_codes[str_to_sn("+", 2)]   = SUM_OP;
%       Op_codes[str_to_sn("mod", 2)] = MOD_OP;        /* ... 26 of these */
%
%   greatest_symnum() returns the current symbol count, while str_to_sn()
%   INTERNS a symbol that is not already in the table and hands back a number
%   past that snapshot.  Every one of the 26 operator symbols the input did
%   not already mention is created right there, and its op code is written off
%   the end of the array.
%
%   The author knew about the hazard: five other places in the same file guard
%   with "if (symnum >= Symbols_size)".  The initialisation block is the one
%   that does not.
%
% WHY IT MATTERS
%   set(production) implies set(eval_rewrite), which is the only caller, so
%   this fires on every production-mode run -- including every
%   production-mode example in the Prover9 manual (2inverter, cabbages, jugs,
%   list, queens3).  It is present in pristine LADR-2009-11A and,
%   independently confirmed, in the current LADR-2026 release.
%
% WHY NOTHING NOTICED FOR SEVENTEEN YEARS
%   The slots written past the end belong to exactly the operators the input
%   never mentions, so nothing reads them back.  Fixed and unfixed builds
%   produce byte-identical output on every example tried.  It is pure heap
%   corruption with no visible symptom: MALLOC_CHECK_=3 does not catch it
%   either.  Only a sanitizer sees it, which is why the regression test for it
%   reports SKIP on an ordinary build rather than a meaningless PASS.
%
% RUN IT
%   An ordinary build shows nothing -- that is the point:
%       bin/prover9 -f test.src/demos/m7-production-overflow.in
%
%   On a build made with -fsanitize=address, the 2009 code reports
%
%       ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow
%       WRITE of size 4
%           #0 init_dollar_eval ladr/dollar.c:75
%           #1 index_and_process_initial_clauses provers.src/search.c:2394
%       0x... is located 0 bytes after 444-byte region
%
%   and this tree reports nothing.  The size of the region depends on the
%   input, since the symbol count does: 444 bytes on the manual's examples,
%   324 on this one.
%
%   Valgrind shows it on the SHIPPED binary with no instrumented build at all,
%   which is the better demonstration:
%       valgrind bin/prover9 -f test.src/demos/m7-production-overflow.in
%------------------------------------------------------------------------------

set(production).
assign(max_seconds,5).

formulas(sos).
  p(1 + 1).
  q(max(3,5)).
end_of_list.
